INSERT INTO `product_dosage` VALUES (3,2,'Direction of Use','Take one oral serving once daily with a meal, preferably containing some dietary fat to support curcumin and CoQ10 absorption. During active chemotherapy or radiotherapy, use antioxidant supplementation only with the treating oncologist’s approval. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:49','2026-09-18 06:12:49'),(4,3,'Direction of Use','Common oncology regimens include 175 mg/m² IV over 3 hours every 3 weeks, or 80 mg/m² IV weekly, depending on tumour and combination regimen. Premedicate for hypersensitivity and check CBC/liver function before each dose. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:49','2026-09-18 06:12:49'),(5,4,'Direction of Use','IV over 30 minutes. Common schedules are 1,000 mg/m² on days 1 and 8 every 21 days, or 1,000 mg/m² on days 1, 8 and 15 every 28 days; some breast regimens use 1,250 mg/m² on days 1 and 8 every 21 days. CBC/organ function guide each cycle. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:49','2026-09-18 06:12:49'),(6,5,'Direction of Use','Typical dosing is 85 mg/m² IV over about 2 hours every 2 weeks in FOLFOX-type regimens, or 130 mg/m² every 3 weeks in some CAPOX regimens. Avoid cold drinks/exposure for several days after infusion because acute neuropathy can be cold-triggered. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(7,6,'Direction of Use','IV infusion every 2–3 weeks; common doses are 5 or 10 mg/kg every 2 weeks, or 7.5 or 15 mg/kg every 3 weeks, depending on cancer/regimen. Check blood pressure, urine protein and wound-healing status. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(8,7,'Direction of Use','For newly diagnosed glioblastoma, a standard regimen is 75 mg/m² once daily during radiotherapy (up to 42 days), then 150–200 mg/m² once daily on days 1–5 of each 28-day maintenance cycle. Take at the same time daily, preferably fasting/at bedtime with antiemetic support. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(9,8,'Direction of Use','A common chemotherapy-support dose is 5 mcg/kg once daily SC (or IV), starting at least 24 hours after cytotoxic chemotherapy and continuing until post-nadir neutrophil recovery. Do not give within 24 hours before or after chemotherapy. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(10,9,'Direction of Use','Take one oral serving once daily after food. For supportive use during cancer care, keep the dose consistent and avoid combining with additional high-dose curcumin or botanical extracts unless reviewed by the treating oncologist. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(11,10,'Direction of Use','Typical tocotrienol supplementation is 100–300 mg per day, taken once daily or in two divided doses with a meal containing fat to improve absorption. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(25,24,'Direction of Use','For allergic rhinitis: age 12+ years, 2 sprays in each nostril once daily initially, reducing to 1 spray/nostril once controlled. Age 6–11 years, start 1 spray/nostril once daily; may increase to 2 sprays/nostril if needed. Prime and aim away from the septum. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(27,26,'Direction of Use','Use 1–2 sprays in each nostril 2–4 times daily or as needed for dryness/congestion. Blow the nose gently first; clean the nozzle after use. It can be used before a medicated nasal spray. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(76,75,'Direction of Use','Take 1 tablet once daily on an empty stomach—at least 1 hour before or 2 hours after food/fruit juice. Evening dosing is convenient when night symptoms are prominent. Reassess the need for montelukast if used only for mild rhinitis. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:51','2026-09-18 06:12:51'),(77,76,'Direction of Use','Place the 4 mg ODT on the tongue and allow it to dissolve. For general adult nausea, 4 mg every 8–12 hours as needed is commonly used; chemotherapy/postoperative regimens differ. In severe hepatic impairment, total ondansetron should not exceed 8 mg/day. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:51','2026-09-18 06:12:51'),(129,128,'Direction of Use','Instil 1 drop in the affected eye twice daily. Use punctal occlusion for 1–2 minutes after dosing. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:52','2026-09-18 06:12:52'),(137,136,'Direction of Use','Take 1 tablet once daily in the evening/at bedtime initially. If pain remains uncontrolled, any increase should be clinician-led; pregabalin must be adjusted in renal impairment and tapered rather than stopped abruptly. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:52','2026-09-18 06:12:52'),(152,151,'Direction of Use','Take 1 tablet once daily in the evening/at bedtime initially. If pain remains uncontrolled, any increase should be clinician-led; pregabalin must be adjusted in renal impairment and tapered rather than stopped abruptly. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:53','2026-09-18 06:12:53'),(153,152,'Direction of Use','Take 1 tablet twice daily after meals for a short course, commonly 3–5 days and generally not more than 7–10 days without review. Avoid additional NSAIDs or paracetamol-containing combinations. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:53','2026-09-18 06:12:53'),(157,155,'Direction of Use','Take 1 tablet twice daily after meals for short-term pain, usually a few days. Do not add another paracetamol or NSAID product without calculating the total daily dose. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:53','2026-09-18 06:12:53'),(158,156,'Direction of Use','Take 1 tablet twice daily after meals for the shortest possible course, typically 3–7 days. Oral thiocolchicoside should not be used long term; stop earlier if pain/spasm resolves. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-18 06:12:53','2026-09-18 06:12:53'),(162,34,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet once daily with or after a meal. Separate calcium by at least 2–4 hours from levothyroxine, tetracyclines and quinolone antibiotics. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(163,35,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet/softgel once daily after a meal. DHA-containing softgels are best taken with food containing some fat. Do not add other high-dose folate/B12 products unless clinically indicated. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(164,36,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet/softgel once daily after a meal. DHA-containing softgels are best taken with food containing some fat. Do not add other high-dose folate/B12 products unless clinically indicated. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(165,37,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Common 10 mg regimens are indication-specific: dysmenorrhoea 10 mg twice daily on cycle days 5–25; irregular cycles 10 mg twice daily on days 11–25; endometriosis 10 mg two to three times daily on days 5–25 or continuously. Pregnancy/luteal-support schedules should be set by the gynaecologist. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(166,38,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet once daily. Best iron absorption is away from tea/coffee/calcium; if nausea occurs, take after food. In iron-deficiency anaemia, continue for roughly 3 months after haemoglobin normalises to replenish stores unless the doctor advises otherwise. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(167,39,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet once daily. Best iron absorption is away from tea/coffee/calcium; if nausea occurs, take after food. In iron-deficiency anaemia, continue for roughly 3 months after haemoglobin normalises to replenish stores unless the doctor advises otherwise. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(168,40,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For PCOS/metabolic support, take one serving once daily with food; if tolerated and clinically intended, twice-daily dosing can be used because trials of myo-inositol commonly provide 2–4 g/day in divided doses. Monitor total magnesium and zinc intake. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(169,41,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For ovulation triggering, 5,000–10,000 IU is usually given as a single IM/SC injection once follicles are mature, typically 24–48 hours after the last gonadotropin dose, with timed intercourse/IUI about 24–36 hours later. Male hypogonadotropic regimens use repeated doses and are specialist-directed. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(171,43,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take a dose delivering 1 g sucralfate (commonly 10 mL of suspension) 3 times daily, 1 hour before meals; a bedtime dose may be added in ulcer regimens. Keep other oral medicines at least 2 hours apart. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(172,44,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For oral micronized progesterone SR, 200–300 mg once daily—usually at bedtime—is commonly used in luteal/pregnancy-support practice. Studies of SR formulations commonly used 300 mg once daily in high-risk pregnancy; exact start/stop dates depend on the obstetric indication. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(173,45,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet twice daily with meals. In PCOS and insulin-resistance studies, myo-inositol is commonly used in total daily doses of 2–4 g, usually divided twice daily; any dose escalation should be medically supervised. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(174,46,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Insert 1 vaginal tablet/suppository high into the vagina at bedtime for 7 consecutive nights. Wash hands before/after insertion, avoid intercourse/tampons during treatment, and do not use during pregnancy without gynaecologist approval. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(175,47,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Dissolve 1 sachet in water and take twice daily (morning and evening), providing 4 g/day myo-inositol if each sachet contains 2 g—the dose commonly used in PCOS studies. Take with or after food if GI upset occurs. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(176,48,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 softgel once daily with food. Because it contains calcitriol 0.25 mcg, serum calcium/phosphate should be monitored in prolonged use; do not combine with high-dose vitamin D without medical supervision. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(177,49,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 capsule once daily for about 4–8 weeks as an adjunct after/alongside indicated BV treatment. If also taking oral antibiotics, separate the probiotic by about 2 hours. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(178,50,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet/capsule once daily with a main meal to improve tolerance and absorption of fat-soluble antioxidants. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(179,51,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet twice daily with plenty of water. This provides 1.2 g of D-mannose per day; recurrent-UTI prevention studies commonly use approximately 2 g/day, so the formulation is best positioned as adjunct urinary-tract support. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(180,52,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Mix one measured serving with water or milk and take once daily, preferably with breakfast or as a snack. Use consistently for at least 8–12 weeks when used as nutritional support for metabolic or reproductive health. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(181,53,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet three times daily after food, starting when heavy menstrual bleeding begins, usually for 3–5 days only. Do not continue beyond the menstrual episode. The fixed combination should not be escalated to high-dose tranexamic-acid regimens because mefenamic-acid exposure would also rise. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(182,11,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Give once daily after a meal. In children, calcium supplementation is generally used to complement dietary intake toward age-appropriate total calcium requirements, while Vitamin D is commonly supplied in the range of 400–600 IU daily depending on age and clinical need. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(183,12,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Give once daily after food. Paediatric zinc supplementation is commonly adjusted to provide approximately 3–10 mg of elemental zinc per day according to age; therapeutic treatment of zinc deficiency may require higher short-term doses under medical supervision. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(185,14,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Give 400 IU once daily. In breastfed infants, 400 IU daily is commonly recommended from the first days of life through at least 12 months, unless the paediatrician recommends a different dose. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(186,15,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Give 1 gummy once daily after a meal to children who can safely chew gummies. Avoid combining with other calcium or Vitamin D supplements unless total daily intake has been reviewed. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(187,16,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For paediatric sleep-onset problems, start low: 1–3 mg 30–60 minutes before the target bedtime. With a 3 mg/5 mL syrup, 1 mg≈1.7 mL, 2 mg≈3.3 mL and 3 mg=5 mL. Use only after sleep-hygiene measures and paediatric assessment. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(188,17,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Give 1 gummy once daily after food. It is best used as nutritional support alongside a balanced diet rather than as a substitute for meals. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(189,18,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Shake well. A common paediatric dose for many susceptible infections is 5 mg/kg per dose every 12 hours (10 mg/kg/day). At 50 mg/5 mL, this equals 0.5 mL/kg per dose; maximum and duration depend on infection (often 5–14 days). Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(191,20,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Mix one standard serving with water or milk and give once daily, preferably between meals or after a meal. Protein supplementation in children should complement, not replace, normal dietary protein intake. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(192,21,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Administer once daily, preferably at the same time each day. Paediatric Lactobacillus rhamnosus products commonly provide about 1–10 billion CFU per day depending on the strain and indication. Shake well before use. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(193,22,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Children aged 2–6 years: 2 mg (commonly 5 mL of a 2 mg/5 mL syrup) two to three times daily, maximum 12 mg/day. Children aged 7–14 years: 4 mg (commonly 10 mL) two to three times daily, maximum 16 mg/day. Start with the lowest effective frequency because sedation is common. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(194,23,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Give one paediatric serving once daily after food. Avoid simultaneous use of multiple multivitamin/mineral products to prevent excessive intake of Vitamin A, zinc, selenium and other micronutrients. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(195,149,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Start with 1 tablet once daily with the main meal for 2–4 weeks to improve diacerein tolerability; if needed and well tolerated, a clinician may increase to 1 tablet twice daily. Stop for persistent diarrhoea or signs of liver injury. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(196,150,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet twice daily after meals for 8–12 weeks, then reassess pain/function and the need for continued supplementation. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:32','2026-09-28 18:53:32'),(199,153,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 capsule once or twice daily with meals for joint-support use. Benefits from collagen/curcumin-type combinations are gradual, so assess after about 8–12 weeks rather than using as an acute pain reliever. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(200,154,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet once daily with a meal. Separate from levothyroxine and tetracycline/quinolone antibiotics by at least 2–4 hours. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(201,1,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 capsule once daily with food. The listed amounts (Aflapin 100 mg, undenatured type II collagen 40 mg and Mobilee 40 mg) correspond to once-daily doses commonly used in joint-support formulations; assess benefit over 8–12 weeks. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(204,157,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet 2–3 times daily on an empty stomach (about 1 hour before or 2 hours after food) for a short course, commonly 5–10 days, unless GI intolerance occurs. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(205,158,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet twice daily after meals for a short course, commonly 3–5 days and generally not beyond 7–10 days without review because of the diclofenac component. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(206,132,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet once daily after food for 8–12 weeks, then reassess the need for ongoing supplementation and the underlying cause of neuropathy/B-vitamin deficiency. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(207,133,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Sublingual tablet: 1,500 mcg once daily, allowed to dissolve under the tongue. Injection: a common replacement approach is 1,000–1,500 mcg IM weekly for about 4 weeks, then monthly if ongoing malabsorption/deficiency requires maintenance. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(208,134,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet/capsule once daily after a meal for about 8–12 weeks, then reassess symptoms and the underlying neuropathy cause. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(209,135,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 SR tablet once daily after the evening meal or at bedtime. Swallow whole; renal impairment may require dose reduction. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(211,137,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Oral citicoline is commonly used at 500 mg once or twice daily. Injectable regimens commonly use 500–1,000 mg/day IV/IM in divided or once-daily dosing; injection should be given by a healthcare professional. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(212,138,'Administration & Usage Guidance','A practical high-dose methylcobalamin injection schedule is 2,500 mcg IM once weekly for 4–6 weeks, then reassess; longer-term maintenance should be based on the cause of B12 deficiency. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(213,139,'Administration & Usage Guidance','A common neuro-vitamin injection schedule is 1 ampoule by IM or slow IV administration 1–3 times weekly for a short correction phase, followed by less frequent injections or oral maintenance depending on the clinical response. Administration should be performed by a healthcare professional. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(214,140,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet twice daily after meals. Reduce or review the dose in renal impairment because piracetam is predominantly renally cleared. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(215,141,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take the 40 mg SR tablet once daily at the same time each day. It is usually a starting/low dose; migraine, tremor and cardiovascular indications may require titration based on pulse, blood pressure and response. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(216,142,'Administration & Usage Guidance','125 mg strength: given IV/IM as a single or repeated dose depending on the acute inflammatory indication. 1,000 mg strength: used for specialist \'pulse\' therapy, commonly 1 g IV once daily for 3–5 days (for example selected neurologic relapses). Continuous monitoring is required. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(217,143,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Start with 1 tablet at night; if needed and tolerated, increase to twice daily and then up to three times daily only under clinician guidance. Gabapentin must be dose-adjusted in renal impairment and tapered when stopping. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(218,144,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet/capsule once daily after a meal for about 8–12 weeks, then reassess symptoms and the underlying neuropathy cause. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(219,145,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take once daily, commonly in the evening during initiation because clonazepam may cause sedation. The clonazepam component is generally limited to the first 2–4 weeks where possible and should be tapered gradually rather than stopped abruptly. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(220,146,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet immediately before bedtime only when 7–8 hours of uninterrupted sleep are available. Standard immediate-release zolpidem dosing is 5–10 mg once nightly in adults, with lower starting doses preferred in older adults and in patients more sensitive to next-day sedation. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(221,147,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 capsule twice daily with meals (600 mg/day PEA) for 4–8 weeks, then reassess pain/function. Some studies use higher PEA exposure, but increasing beyond this should be clinician-led. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(222,148,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 capsule 30–60 minutes before bedtime. Avoid alcohol and other sedatives; reassess if used nightly for more than a few weeks. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:33','2026-09-28 18:53:33'),(223,105,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1 drop in the affected eye 3 times daily for 7 days for uncomplicated bacterial conjunctivitis. Remove contact lenses during active infection and avoid touching the bottle tip. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(224,106,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For gatifloxacin 0.5% bacterial conjunctivitis: days 1–2, instil 1 drop every 2 hours while awake (up to 8 times/day); days 3–7, 1 drop 2–4 times daily. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(225,107,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For postoperative/infective inflammation, a common practical regimen is 1 drop 4 times daily for 7–14 days, then review. Separate from other eye drops by at least 5 minutes. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(226,108,'Administration & Usage Guidance','A common postoperative regimen is 1 drop 4 times daily initially. Review within 7 days; the antibiotic component is usually limited to about 1 week, while the steroid may need tapering based on inflammation and intraocular pressure. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(227,109,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1–2 drops in the affected eye 4 times daily. After eye surgery, treatment commonly starts about 24 hours post-op and continues for up to 2 weeks, with review before extension. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(228,110,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1 drop (or 1–2 drops depending on bottle instructions) every 4–6 hours; in severe inflammation some regimens start more frequently for 24–48 hours. Review within 5–7 days and do not continue a steroid/antibiotic combination unsupervised. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(229,111,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1 drop (or 1–2 drops depending on bottle instructions) every 4–6 hours; in severe inflammation some regimens start more frequently for 24–48 hours. Review within 5–7 days and do not continue a steroid/antibiotic combination unsupervised. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(230,112,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1 drop (or 1–2 drops depending on bottle instructions) every 4–6 hours; in severe inflammation some regimens start more frequently for 24–48 hours. Review within 5–7 days and do not continue a steroid/antibiotic combination unsupervised. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(231,113,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1 drop in the affected eye twice daily, about 12 hours apart. After instillation, close the eye and press the inner corner for 1–2 minutes to reduce systemic timolol absorption. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(232,229,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1 drop in the affected eye twice daily, approximately 12 hours apart. Use punctal occlusion for 1–2 minutes after each dose. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(233,115,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For nepafenac 0.1% around cataract surgery, instil 1 drop in the affected eye 3 times daily starting 1 day before surgery, on the day of surgery and for about 2 weeks afterward. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(234,116,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1 drop in each affected eye twice daily, about 6–8 hours apart, during the allergy period. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(235,117,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1–2 drops in each affected eye 3–4 times daily or as needed for dryness; separate from medicated eye drops by at least 5 minutes. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(236,118,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1–2 drops in each affected eye as needed, commonly 3–6 times daily. If needed very frequently, consider a preservative-free lubricant. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(237,119,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1–2 drops in each affected eye 3–4 times daily or as needed for dryness; separate from medicated eye drops by at least 5 minutes. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(238,120,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1 drop in each affected eye 3–4 times daily, or more often if advised for significant dry eye. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(239,121,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1–2 drops in each affected eye 3–4 times daily or as needed for dryness; separate from medicated eye drops by at least 5 minutes. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(240,122,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For bromfenac 0.09% ophthalmic therapy after cataract surgery, instil 1 drop into the affected eye once daily beginning 1 day before surgery, continue on the day of surgery, and continue for the first 14 days after surgery. Keep other eye drops at least 5 minutes apart. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(241,123,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 softgel once daily with a meal containing fat to improve absorption of lutein, zeaxanthin, astaxanthin and vitamin E. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(242,124,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1 drop in the affected eye 3 times daily, approximately 8 hours apart. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(243,125,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Because this is a gatifloxacin/ketorolac fixed combination, a common postoperative/infective regimen is 1 drop 4 times daily for about 7–14 days, with ophthalmic review if symptoms persist. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(244,126,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1 drop in the affected eye 3 times daily, roughly 8 hours apart. Use punctal occlusion for 1–2 minutes. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(245,127,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For prevention of intraoperative miosis, a standard flurbiprofen 0.03% regimen is 1 drop every 30 minutes starting about 2 hours before surgery (total 4 drops). Other uses require an ophthalmologist-defined regimen. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(246,114,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1 drop in the affected eye twice daily. Use punctal occlusion for 1–2 minutes after dosing. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(247,129,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Instil 1 drop 4 times daily for about 7 days, then reassess. If the steroid needs to continue, the dose should be tapered according to inflammation and intraocular pressure. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(248,130,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For fungal keratitis, natamycin 5% is often started at 1 drop every 1–2 hours while awake for the first 3–4 days, then reduced to 6–8 times daily; total therapy commonly lasts 14–21 days or longer according to corneal response. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(249,131,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For diagnostic dilation, instil 1 drop in the eye; repeat once after 5–10 minutes if required. Examination is usually performed 15–30 minutes later. This is generally clinic-administered. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(250,77,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a very thin layer to the affected skin once or twice daily for no more than about 5–7 days unless a dermatologist specifically extends it. Because it contains clobetasol, do not use it as routine treatment for uncomplicated fungal rash. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(251,78,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a thin layer once daily to the lesion and about 2.5 cm of surrounding skin: 1 week for tinea corporis/cruris; 2 weeks for interdigital tinea pedis. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(252,79,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a thin layer to affected skin twice daily until clear. For recurrent atopic dermatitis, maintenance twice weekly to previously affected areas may be used after control, if directed by the dermatologist. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:34','2026-09-28 18:53:34'),(253,80,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply generously to exposed skin about 15 minutes before sun exposure (roughly 2 mg/cm²; about 2 finger-lengths for the face/neck). Reapply every 2 hours and immediately after swimming, sweating or towel drying. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(254,81,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 20 mg once daily, with or without food. Use at the same time each day during symptomatic periods. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(255,82,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet once daily after a meal for 8–12 weeks before judging hair/nail response, while investigating iron, thyroid or other causes of hair loss where relevant. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(256,83,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a pea-sized amount as a thin film once nightly for the first week; if well tolerated, increase to twice daily. Use moisturiser and non-comedogenic sunscreen. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(257,84,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Use 2 sprays inside the mouth twice daily after meals. Hold the liquid in the mouth briefly before swallowing and avoid eating or drinking for about 15 minutes afterward. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(258,85,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply liberally to dry skin 2–4 times daily and after bathing/hand washing. It can be used more frequently during eczema flares as a moisturiser. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(259,86,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a small amount to the affected area 3 times daily for up to 10 days. Reassess if there is no clear improvement within 3–5 days. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(260,87,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a thin layer to itchy/irritated skin 2–3 times daily as needed. Do not apply to infected, weeping or broken skin unless advised. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(261,88,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For short inflammatory/allergic courses, 6–18 mg once daily after breakfast is a common low-to-moderate adult range, but the exact dose depends on diagnosis. Courses longer than about 1–2 weeks generally require tapering rather than abrupt stopping. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(262,89,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For allergic rhinitis, 120 mg once daily is commonly used; for chronic urticaria, 180 mg once daily. Take with water and avoid grapefruit/orange/apple juice close to the dose. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(263,90,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Common adult schedules are 500 mg once daily for 3 days, or 500 mg on day 1 followed by 250 mg once daily on days 2–5, depending on infection. Not every infection is appropriate for azithromycin. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(264,91,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Wet the face, massage a small amount for 30–60 seconds, then rinse. Use once daily initially; increase to twice daily if the skin remains comfortable. Follow with moisturiser and sunscreen. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(265,92,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet/capsule once daily with a main meal. Avoid combining with multiple high-dose antioxidant products unless specifically indicated. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(266,93,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a very thin layer to the pigmented area once nightly for a limited course, typically 8–12 weeks, with strict broad-spectrum sunscreen every morning. Do not use continuously for months without dermatology review. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(267,94,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a pea-sized amount to the entire acne-prone area once nightly. Start every other night for 1 week if sensitive, then nightly. Limit prolonged topical-antibiotic exposure; review at about 8–12 weeks. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(268,95,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a very thin layer once daily (occasionally twice daily for very thick plaques) for up to 2 weeks, then stop or step down. Avoid face, groin, axillae and large body areas. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(269,96,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a thin layer twice daily for about 5–7 days only on clinician-confirmed inflamed mixed infection. If fungal treatment must continue, step down to a plain antifungal rather than continuing the steroid combination. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(270,97,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a thin layer 3–4 times daily for 7–14 days; shorter courses are preferred when clinically adequate. If covered with a dressing, less frequent application may be sufficient. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(271,98,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a thin layer once nightly to clean, dry hyperpigmented areas. For sensitive skin, begin on alternate nights for the first 1–2 weeks, then increase to nightly use if well tolerated. Apply broad-spectrum sunscreen every morning. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(272,99,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply 2–3 drops to clean, dry hyperpigmented areas once nightly; if well tolerated, it may be increased to twice daily. Use sunscreen every morning because depigmenting treatment is ineffective without UV protection. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(273,100,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet/capsule once daily with a main meal. Avoid combining with multiple high-dose antioxidant products unless specifically indicated. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(274,101,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a thin layer to the acne-prone area twice daily after cleansing for up to about 8–12 weeks. Consider concurrent benzoyl peroxide (separate product) to reduce clindamycin resistance if the dermatologist agrees. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(275,102,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a very thin layer once or twice daily for only 5–7 days unless a dermatologist specifically advises otherwise. Avoid face/groin/skin folds because clobetasol is very potent. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(276,103,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Apply a thin layer (about 2–4 g depending on area) 3–4 times daily to intact skin for up to 7–14 days. Wash hands after application and avoid heating pads/occlusive dressings. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(277,104,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Use 2–3 times weekly for 2–4 weeks. Massage into wet scalp, leave in place for 3–5 minutes, then rinse thoroughly; after control, use once weekly or every 1–2 weeks for maintenance. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:35','2026-09-28 18:53:35'),(278,13,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For allergic rhinitis: age 12+ years, 2 sprays in each nostril once daily initially, reducing to 1 spray/nostril once controlled. Age 6–11 years, start 1 spray/nostril once daily; may increase to 2 sprays/nostril if needed. Prime and aim away from the septum. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(279,25,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For short inflammatory/allergic courses, 6–18 mg once daily after breakfast is a common low-to-moderate adult range, but the exact dose depends on diagnosis. Courses longer than about 1–2 weeks generally require tapering rather than abrupt stopping. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(280,19,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Use 1–2 sprays in each nostril 2–4 times daily or as needed for dryness/congestion. Blow the nose gently first; clean the nozzle after use. It can be used before a medicated nasal spray. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(281,27,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Snip open 1 capsule and squeeze the liquid into about 0.5 L hot water; inhale vapour gently for 5–10 minutes. Alternatively put the liquid on a tissue/handkerchief or pillow. Use up to 3 times daily. Do not swallow the capsule. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(282,28,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take at the start of a meal. Typical adult use is 625 mg every 8 hours or a 1,000 mg-strength formulation every 12 hours for about 5–7 days, depending on infection and renal function. Complete the prescribed course. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(283,29,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Use 1 spray in each nostril twice daily (morning and evening). Blow the nose first, shake/prime the spray, and aim slightly outward away from the septum. Once symptoms are controlled, step down only if the prescriber recommends it. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(285,31,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 20 mg once daily on an empty stomach, at least 1 hour before or 2 hours after food or fruit juice. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(286,32,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Adults and older children commonly take 5–10 mL two to three times daily after meals for short-term symptomatic cough support. In younger children, use an age-appropriate reduced dose under paediatric supervision. If cough persists beyond 5–7 days, is associated with wheezing, fever or breathing difficulty, seek medical review. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(287,33,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet or capsule once daily with food. When a divided regimen is clinically preferred, it may be taken twice daily with meals. Avoid taking bromelain- or berberine-containing products on an empty stomach if they cause gastrointestinal discomfort. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(288,54,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 40 mg once daily 30–60 minutes before breakfast; for selected refractory acid disorders a clinician may use twice-daily therapy. Typical courses are 4–8 weeks before reassessment. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(289,55,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 capsule once daily 15–30 minutes before breakfast. Because the formulation contains 30 mg domperidone, keep treatment as short as possible—often days to 1–2 weeks—unless a clinician specifically extends it. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(290,56,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take tablets with food. Typical adult/adolescent dosing is 100 mg every 12 hours for pharyngitis or uncomplicated UTI, and 200 mg every 12 hours for sinusitis, pneumonia or bronchitis; duration is usually 5–14 days depending on infection. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(291,57,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet every 12 hours with food for a clinician-defined course, commonly 5–10 days depending on infection. Renal impairment may require interval adjustment. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(292,58,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet twice daily after meals for short-term pain, usually a few days. Do not add another paracetamol or NSAID product without calculating the total daily dose. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(293,59,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet twice daily after meals for a short course, commonly 3–5 days and generally not more than 7–10 days without review. Avoid additional NSAIDs or paracetamol-containing combinations. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(294,60,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet twice daily after meals for the shortest possible course, typically 3–7 days. Oral thiocolchicoside should not be used long term; stop earlier if pain/spasm resolves. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(295,61,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet once daily in the evening/at bedtime initially. If pain remains uncontrolled, any increase should be clinician-led; pregabalin must be adjusted in renal impairment and tapered rather than stopped abruptly. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(296,62,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For adult constipation, start with 15–30 mL once daily or in two divided doses and adjust to achieve 1–2 soft stools per day. For hepatic encephalopathy, 30–45 mL three to four times daily is commonly titrated to achieve 2–3 soft stools daily. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(297,63,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take a dose delivering 1 g sucralfate (commonly 10 mL of suspension) 3 times daily, 1 hour before meals; a bedtime dose may be added in ulcer regimens. Keep other oral medicines at least 2 hours apart. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(298,64,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 softgel once daily with a meal for 2–4 weeks; if used with antibiotics, take it at least 2 hours before or after the antibiotic. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:36','2026-09-28 18:53:36'),(299,65,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Oral rabeprazole 20 mg: take once daily about 30 minutes before breakfast; common GERD/ulcer courses are 4–8 weeks. If the injectable form is used because oral therapy is not possible, 20 mg IV once daily is a common acid-suppression regimen until oral treatment can resume. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(300,66,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 capsule once daily 15–30 minutes before breakfast. Keep the domperidone-containing course short (often up to 1 week for nausea/motility symptoms) and reassess before longer use. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(301,67,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 capsule once daily, preferably 30 minutes before breakfast. Use for the shortest duration needed; reassess if used beyond 2–4 weeks because levosulpiride can raise prolactin and cause movement symptoms. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(302,68,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 SR capsule once daily before breakfast or the main meal, about 30 minutes before food. Reassess after 2–4 weeks rather than using indefinitely. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(303,69,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 40 mg once daily 30–60 minutes before breakfast. Use 4–8 weeks for common acid-related indications, then step down/stop if clinically appropriate. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(304,70,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 capsule once daily 15–30 minutes before breakfast. The domperidone component should generally be short term and reviewed if symptoms persist. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(305,71,'Administration & Usage Guidance','A practical male-fertility/sexual-wellness adjunct schedule is 1 tablet twice daily after meals for at least 8–12 weeks before judging response, because spermatogenesis takes roughly 2–3 months. Do not use as a substitute for infertility evaluation. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(306,72,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 250 mg every 12 hours for 5–10 days for susceptible infections, with duration depending on diagnosis. Tablets may be taken with or without food, but taking after food can improve absorption/tolerance. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(307,73,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 500 mg every 12 hours for 5–10 days for susceptible infections, with duration depending on diagnosis. Tablets may be taken with or without food, but taking after food can improve absorption/tolerance. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(308,74,'Administration & Usage Guidance','For adults, fixed-dose cefuroxime/clavulanate combinations are commonly taken as 1 tablet every 12 hours after food for about 5–10 days, depending on the infection. Paediatric treatment should be weight-based. Complete the full prescribed course. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(309,30,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet once daily on an empty stomach—at least 1 hour before or 2 hours after food/fruit juice. Evening dosing is convenient when night symptoms are prominent. Reassess the need for montelukast if used only for mild rhinitis. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(310,42,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Place the 4 mg ODT on the tongue and allow it to dissolve. For general adult nausea, 4 mg every 8–12 hours as needed is commonly used; chemotherapy/postoperative regimens differ. In severe hepatic impairment, total ondansetron should not exceed 8 mg/day. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(311,308,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Mix 1 scoop in 200 mL of water or milk once or twice daily as recommended by the clinical oncologist or dietitian. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(312,309,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet (4 mg) 30 minutes before initiation of chemotherapy, followed by 4 mg every 8 hours for 1 to 2 days after completion of chemotherapy. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(313,310,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 1 tablet (8 mg) 30 to 60 minutes prior to chemotherapy, repeated 8 to 12 hours later, then 8 mg twice daily for 1 to 2 days post-chemotherapy. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(314,311,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Administered as a daily subcutaneous injection or intravenous infusion starting at least 24 hours after cytotoxic chemotherapy until expected neutrophil nadir has passed and count has normalized. Administer under clinical supervision.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(315,312,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Take 125 mg orally 1 hour before chemotherapy on Day 1, followed by 80 mg once daily in the morning on Days 2 and 3. Swallow whole with water. Use as prescribed by the doctor.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37'),(316,313,'Administration & Usage Guidance','Administered as a single intravenous bolus (0.25 mg) over 30 seconds approximately 30 minutes prior to the start of chemotherapy. Administered in hospital/clinic settings under medical supervision.','2026-09-28 18:53:37','2026-09-28 18:53:37');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `product_dosage` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;

--
-- Table structure for table `product_mechanisms`
--

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS `product_mechanisms`;
/*!40101 SET @saved_cs_client     = @@character_set_client */;
/*!50503 SET character_set_client = utf8mb4 */;
CREATE TABLE `product_mechanisms` (
  `id` int unsigned NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,
  `product_id` int unsigned NOT NULL,
  `title` varchar(150) COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL,
  `description` text COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL,
  `display_order` int NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',
  `created_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  `updated_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),
  KEY `fk_mechanisms_product` (`product_id`),
  CONSTRAINT `fk_mechanisms_product` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `products` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE
) ENGINE=InnoDB AUTO_INCREMENT=314 DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
/*!40101 SET character_set_client = @saved_cs_client */;

--
-- Dumping data for table `product_mechanisms`
--

LOCK TABLES `product_mechanisms` WRITE;
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `product_mechanisms` DISABLE KEYS */;
INSERT INTO `product_mechanisms` VALUES (1,2,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Curcuminoids modulate oxidative and inflammatory signalling (including NF-κB-related pathways), while CoQ10 participates in mitochondrial electron transport and lipid-phase antioxidant protection. Nano/water-soluble forms are intended to improve oral dispersion and exposure.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:49','2026-09-18 06:12:49'),(2,3,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Paclitaxel binds beta-tubulin and stabilizes microtubules. This prevents the normal microtubule disassembly required for mitosis, arrests dividing cells and ultimately promotes cancer-cell death.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:49','2026-09-18 06:12:49'),(3,4,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Inside cells it is converted to active nucleoside metabolites that inhibit DNA synthesis and ribonucleotide reductase, causing replication stress and death of rapidly dividing cells.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:49','2026-09-18 06:12:49'),(4,5,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Forms platinum-DNA crosslinks that distort DNA and block replication/transcription, triggering apoptosis. Its cytotoxicity is not limited to a single cell-cycle phase.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(5,6,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Binds vascular endothelial growth factor A (VEGF-A), reducing VEGF receptor activation and new blood-vessel formation needed for tumour growth.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(6,7,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Spontaneously converts to MTIC, which methylates DNA (especially at guanine residues). Persistent DNA damage can trigger tumour-cell death, particularly when repair pathways are deficient.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(7,8,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Stimulates G-CSF receptors on bone-marrow myeloid progenitor cells, increasing production and release of functional neutrophils.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(8,9,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Curcuminoids and triterpenoid fractions can influence inflammatory and oxidative-stress signalling; bacosides have antioxidant and neuroactive effects in experimental/clinical nutrition research; pectin acts mainly as soluble fibre/prebiotic substrate.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(9,10,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Gamma- and delta-tocotrienols are vitamin E isoforms that intercept lipid free radicals in cell membranes and can modulate inflammatory and cholesterol-synthesis pathways.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(23,24,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Activates glucocorticoid receptors and suppresses multiple inflammatory mediators, reducing nasal congestion, sneezing, itching and rhinorrhoea.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(25,26,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Saline thins mucus, reduces crusting and mechanically washes allergens/irritants from the nasal cavity.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:50','2026-09-18 06:12:50'),(74,75,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Bilastine blocks peripheral H1 receptors; montelukast blocks cysteinyl-leukotriene CysLT1 receptors, reducing allergic inflammation and bronchoconstrictive signalling.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:51','2026-09-18 06:12:51'),(75,76,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Blocks serotonin 5-HT3 receptors on vagal afferents and in central vomiting pathways, reducing nausea and vomiting signalling.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:51','2026-09-18 06:12:51'),(127,128,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Beta-blockers reduce aqueous-humour production; alpha-2 agonists reduce production and increase outflow; carbonic-anhydrase inhibitors reduce bicarbonate-dependent aqueous secretion.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:52','2026-09-18 06:12:52'),(135,136,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Pregabalin binds the alpha2-delta subunit of voltage-gated calcium channels and reduces excitatory neurotransmitter release. Nortriptyline inhibits norepinephrine/serotonin reuptake and modulates descending pain pathways.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:52','2026-09-18 06:12:52'),(150,151,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Pregabalin binds the alpha2-delta subunit of voltage-gated calcium channels and reduces excitatory neurotransmitter release. Nortriptyline inhibits norepinephrine/serotonin reuptake and modulates descending pain pathways.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:53','2026-09-18 06:12:53'),(151,152,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Aceclofenac inhibits prostaglandin synthesis; paracetamol provides additional analgesia; serratiopeptidase is a proteolytic enzyme marketed to reduce inflammatory oedema, though evidence varies by indication.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:53','2026-09-18 06:12:53'),(155,155,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Aceclofenac reduces peripheral prostaglandin-mediated inflammation; paracetamol mainly provides central analgesic and antipyretic effects.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:53','2026-09-18 06:12:53'),(156,156,'How the Formula Works in the Body','Aceclofenac reduces prostaglandin synthesis via COX inhibition; paracetamol adds central analgesic/antipyretic activity; thiocolchicoside acts as a muscle relaxant through glycinergic/GABA-related mechanisms.',1,'2026-09-18 06:12:53','2026-09-18 06:12:53'),(159,34,'Mechanism of Action','Calcium provides substrate for hydroxyapatite; Vitamin D increases intestinal calcium/phosphate absorption; Vitamin K2 supports gamma-carboxylation of proteins such as osteocalcin involved in bone mineral handling.',1,'2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(160,35,'Mechanism of Action','Methylcobalamin serves as an active coenzyme form of vitamin B12 for methionine synthase and myelin-related metabolism; folate/B6 cofactors support one-carbon and homocysteine pathways.',1,'2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(161,36,'Mechanism of Action','Methylcobalamin serves as an active coenzyme form of vitamin B12 for methionine synthase and myelin-related metabolism; folate/B6 cofactors support one-carbon and homocysteine pathways.',1,'2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(162,37,'Mechanism of Action','Binds progesterone receptors and provides progestational effects on the endometrium without meaningful androgenic or estrogenic activity.',1,'2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(163,38,'Mechanism of Action','Iron is incorporated into haemoglobin; folate and B12 support DNA synthesis and erythropoiesis. Chelated/bisglycinate forms may improve gastrointestinal tolerability for some users.',1,'2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(164,39,'Mechanism of Action','Methylcobalamin serves as an active coenzyme form of vitamin B12 for methionine synthase and myelin-related metabolism; folate/B6 cofactors support one-carbon and homocysteine pathways.',1,'2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(165,40,'Mechanism of Action','Calcium provides substrate for hydroxyapatite; Vitamin D increases intestinal calcium/phosphate absorption; Vitamin K2 supports gamma-carboxylation of proteins such as osteocalcin involved in bone mineral handling.',1,'2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(166,41,'Mechanism of Action','Binds LH/hCG receptors. In women it triggers final follicular maturation/ovulation; in men it stimulates Leydig cells to produce testosterone.',1,'2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(168,43,'Mechanism of Action','Sucralfate polymerizes in acidic conditions and adheres to ulcerated mucosa, forming a protective barrier. Oxetacaine locally reduces pain sensation on the gastric/oesophageal mucosa.',1,'2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(169,44,'Mechanism of Action','Activates progesterone receptors, converting the endometrium to a secretory state, supporting luteal/endometrial function and reducing estrogen-driven endometrial proliferation.',1,'2026-09-28 18:53:31','2026-09-28 18:53:31'),(170,45,'Mechanism of Action','Calcium provides substrate for hydroxyapatite; Vitamin D increases intestinal calcium/phosphate absorption; Vitamin K2 supports gamma-carboxylati